{
  "feedback": "Decision: revise. The rationale says sensor_size goes from 0.012 to 0.016 m, but the geometry field still reads 0.012. The candidate's controller is the iteration 4 design (kp 7.0, kd 0.2, ki 0.0, base_speed 1.4), and iteration 4 already raced at 45.59 with sensor_size 0.012. Racing it unchanged would repeat that result and test nothing new, so the sensor change has to be in the field before the race.\n\nEvidence. Across the raced designs, progress tracks kp: kp 6 gave oval progress 0.12, kp 7 gave 0.19, and kp 8 gave 0.18 (scores 36.05, 45.59 and 49.78). Oscillation at kp 7 was 0.128 on the oval, below the 0.13–0.15 seen at kp 8. Every raced run ended off_track with about one line-loss event and max_error of 0.060 to 0.066 m. The s-bend progress was flat at about 0.04 for kp 5, 6 and 7, which points to a geometric stall rather than gain. The 12 mm footprint on 25 mm tape with 0.02 m sensor spacing is a plausible dead band near centre, so changing sensor_size is the next single-group test.\n\nWhat to do next, depending on the race. (a) If max_error falls clearly below 0.06 m, or s-bend progress rises above 0.04, the dead band was the limit: keep sensor_size 0.016 and move to kp 6.5 or outer sensors at x = ±0.06 in a later single-group revision, to cut oscillation. (b) If max_error and s-bend progress do not change, the stall is at a bend the sensors cannot follow: test outer sensors at x = ±0.06 with sensor_size 0.016. (c) If the robot tracks without an off-track event but completion_time exceeds 3 s, raise base_speed to 1.6 in a later single-group revision.",
  "requested_changes": [
    "Set geometry.sensor_size to 0.016. The field must match the rationale, since the current value of 0.012 means this race would just repeat iteration 4 (45.59). Keep every other field unchanged: kp 7.0, kd 0.2, ki 0.0, base_speed 1.4, line_loss last_direction, sensor positions and weights.",
    "Keep the sensor positions at x = -0.04, -0.02, 0.0, 0.02, 0.04 with y = 0.04 for this race. Moving the outer sensors is the next step only if sensor_size 0.016 leaves max_error near 0.06 m on the oval (iteration 4 max_error 0.063).",
    "Report progress, max_error and line_loss_events per track, steering_oscillation, completion_time and rms_error, so the race separates offset from oscillation and shows whether the s-bend stall (flat at about 0.04 across kp 5–7) moves."
  ],
